Error Correcting Codes
- System where you add redundance to data so that it can be recoverable even if it is corrupted
- EE + Information Theory
  - Probabilistic/Randomized Model
- TCS
  - Worst Case Model
- Formal Definition:
  - An injective map that encodes strings such that strings of length k are encoded into strings of length n 
    - The strings are comprised of letters from the same alphabet, call it SIGMA, with Sigma^k denoting a string of length k which is comprised of letters from Sigma
    - The cardinality of Sigma is called q (often times it is 2 as information is transferred in bits)
    - The set of all possible messages that can be sent (domain) is called the MESSAGE SPACE
    - k is the message length or dimension
    - The set of all possible messages that can be outputted (range) is denoted as C
    - If y is in C, then is it a CODEWORD
    - n is the block length
      - Note that n >= k since we are adding redundancies
    - k/n is called RATE
      - Want to add less redundancy for efficiency purposes => k should be close to n (i.e rate is close to 1)
- Errors
  - Should expect errors as it is built to reverse them
  - Assume that it will only be changing characters and not modifying the length
  - If putting string x into the map gives string y, we expect to obtain a string z with the same length as y
    - Want to decode z into x. 
    - Maybe like a matrix transformation that maps R^k to R^n, where k < n, that maps x to y?
      - Find and inverse that maps y to x
